  ✕ `Ref<int>` has no zero value
   ╭─[test.lis:3:11]
 2 │ fn test() {
 3 │   let r = zero<Ref<int>>()
   ·           ────────┬───────
   ·                   ╰── `Ref<int>` does not satisfy `Zeroable`
 4 │ }
   ╰────
  help: `Zeroable` admits only types whose zero value Lisette can produce, and `Ref<int>` has none. Build this value explicitly instead, e.g. `Map.new<K, V>()` for a map or `Channel.new<T>()` for a channel · code: [infer.not_zeroable_bound]
